sieve-filter-v2
; key-data-v2 for the notes3 family: every note in one key, at any length and loudness; rests
; always pass. On a notes3 line a symbol is a note (its pitch from LOW, its level, its length in
; ticks) or a rest (its length), written NOTE(p, k, n) and REST(n). The notes of one pitch, at
; every level and length, are one run of symbols, NOTE(p, 1, 1) to NOTE(p, LEVELS, LONGEST), and
; the rests another, REST(1) to REST(LONGEST).
id        key-notes3
version   1
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     audio
symbols   notes3*
describe  Every note is in the key: its pitch class is in the scale on the tonic. Rests always pass.
param     tonic  choice C C,C#,D,D#,E,F,F#,G,G#,A,A#,B the key's first note
param     scale  choice major major,minor,harmonic-minor,major-pentatonic,minor-pentatonic,blues the scale's notes

states    1
start     0
accept    0
t 0 @{REST(1)}..@{REST(LONGEST)} 0
for p 1 {PITCHES}
  for r {(LOW + p - 1 + 12 - tonic) % 12} {(LOW + p - 1 + 12 - tonic) % 12}
    if {(scale == 0 && (r == 0 || r == 2 || r == 4 || r == 5 || r == 7 || r == 9 || r == 11)) || (scale == 1 && (r == 0 || r == 2 || r == 3 || r == 5 || r == 7 || r == 8 || r == 10)) || (scale == 2 && (r == 0 || r == 2 || r == 3 || r == 5 || r == 7 || r == 8 || r == 11)) || (scale == 3 && (r == 0 || r == 2 || r == 4 || r == 7 || r == 9)) || (scale == 4 && (r == 0 || r == 3 || r == 5 || r == 7 || r == 10)) || (scale == 5 && (r == 0 || r == 3 || r == 5 || r == 6 || r == 7 || r == 10))}
      t 0 @{NOTE(p, 1, 1)}..@{NOTE(p, LEVELS, LONGEST)} 0
    fi
  done
done
end
